  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize digging out the 2s and 3s. Since 2s are buried, you can't build your foundations. Look for moves that uncover low cards.\n\nThe 'Empty Slot' Gambit: Don't fill an empty wing space unless it helps you unblock another pile. An empty space is a 'virtual cell' that lets you shuttle cards around.\n\nReverse Building: Before moving a card to a foundation, check if you need it in the Tableau to hold a lower card. Sometimes keeping a 5 on the board allows you to stack a 4 on it, clearing space elsewhere.",
    Player: "Prioritize digging out the 2s and 3s. Since 2s are buried, you can't build your foundations. Look for moves that uncover low cards.\n\nThe 'Empty Slot' Gambit: Don't fill an empty wing space unless it helps you unblock another pile. An empty space is a 'virtual cell' that lets you shuttle cards around.\n\nReverse Building: Before moving a card to a foundation, check if you need it in the Tableau to hold a lower card. Sometimes keeping a 5 on the board allows you to stack a 4 on it, clearing space elsewhere.",
